---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import Arrow from '../components/Arrow.astro'
import Stage from '../components/Stage.astro'
import { site } from '../site'

const description = 'John DeLong on faith, family, engineering leadership, and the things he builds on the side.'
---

<Base title="About" description={description}>
  <section class="wrap section" style="padding-top: 88px">
    <div class="cols center">
      <div class="s7 stack" style="--gap: 24px">
        <h1 class="h1 in">Hi, I'm <em>{site.author}.</em></h1>
        <p class="lede in" style="--i: 1; font-size: 21px">
          I'm a Christian, a husband, and a dad to three girls. I lead a software team for work,
          and in my spare time I'm usually building something.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="s5 portrait-stage">
        <Stage aspectRatio={3 / 2}>
          <img src="/john-delong.webp" alt={`Portrait of ${site.author}`} width="1200" height="800" />
        </Stage>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section">
    <div class="cols">
      <h2 class="h2 s4 rvl">Faith and family</h2>
      <div class="prose s7 end rv">
        <p>
          My Christian faith is the foundation I build my life around. I believe the Bible is God's Word,
          and I want it to shape how I love my family, how I lead, and how I treat the people around me.
        </p>
        <p>
          I want to make time for God and help our girls grow in their own faith. I also want them to know
          they can come to me about anything. I hope to be someone they still want to talk to and ask for
          advice when they're grown.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section">
    <div class="cols">
      <h2 class="h2 s4 rvl">Work</h2>
      <div class="prose s7 end rv">
        <p>
          I grew up in Cedar Springs, Michigan, and studied computer engineering at Grand Valley State
          University. I started at Dematic, working on software for logistics sites, then spent eleven
          years at Michigan Software Labs. I went from developer to tech lead to leading the development practice.
        </p>
        <h3>LandstarOne</h3>
        <p>
          I spent about seven years building and evolving Landstar's iOS and Android app. On iOS,
          I led the move from UIKit to SwiftUI, using the migration to improve accessibility and support
          larger text across the app.
        </p>
        <h3>Altus Virtual Care</h3>
        <p>
          I spent about a year building a web app that connects hospital patients with doctors and family.
          The system ran on AWS and included video calls, remote camera controls, and an Epic integration.
          I helped get it to launch before handing it over to the Altus team.
        </p>
        <h3>National Heritage Academies</h3>
        <p>
          I now lead the school applications engineering team at National Heritage Academies. We build
          software that schools use to manage student information. I like staying close to the technical
          work, and I try to lead by listening first, clearing roadblocks, and giving people room to do good work.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section">
    <div class="cols">
      <h2 class="h2 s4 rvl">On the side</h2>
      <div class="prose s7 end rv">
        <p>
          A lot of my side projects start with someone I know. <a href="/apps/trellis/">Trellis</a> grew out
          of wanting clearer career paths for the people I lead. <a href="/apps/oriel/">Oriel</a> gave our kids
          a way to see the family calendar for themselves. <a href="/apps/kids-town/">Kids Town</a> started
          when my girls set up a library and handed me a card to check out a book.
        </p>
        <p>
          Away from the keyboard, I like photography, making videos, and building things around the house.
          I've wired entire homes, installed a kitchen, insulated a house, remodeled bathrooms and a basement,
          and built a deck and floating shelves, to name a few projects. I also design and 3D-print things,
          including RC planes I get to fly, and I like trying to get better at latte art.
        </p>
        <p>
          Sidelong means from the side. It fits the things I make on the side and the fun of coming at a
          problem from a slightly different angle.
        </p>
        <a class="link" href="/apps/">See the apps <Arrow /></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap" style="padding-bottom: 96px">
    <div class="cols">
      <h2 class="h2 s4 rvl">Find me</h2>
      <div class="s7 end rv profile-links">
        {site.contact.filter((item) => item.href !== '#').map((item) => (
          <a class="link" href={item.href}>{item.label}</a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .portrait-stage img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 14px;
  }

  .profile-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px 28px;
  }

  .profile-links a {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.25em;
  }
</style>
